{{!
    @template block_compass/block

    The block shell: one React mount point, and nothing else of the block's own. Every
    tier, tier 3 included, renders inside the component.

    The props arrive already JSON-encoded from the renderable, in one value, through a
    triple stash: the quote helper corrupts any value carrying a doubled-brace pair, and
    json_encode() in the renderable does not. Nothing between here and React is an HTML
    context, so a double stash would reach the reader as literal entities.

    The section's trailing content is what a reader sees if the component never
    mounts, which is silent apart from a console message. It says the block could not
    load, which is then true, and offers nothing to press. Only the mounted component
    renders course cards, so a step asserting a course name asserts that React ran.

    The noscript beside it covers the other way this block shows nothing. With
    JavaScript off both messages appear, and both are true: one says what happened,
    the other says why.

    The mount point names the bundle: one ES module built from Block.tsx by a build step
    outside core's grunt, opted into by js/esm/bundle.json, so the client arrives in one
    request rather than one per module. The per-file outputs stay in js/esm/build for
    core's own build check and are imported by nothing.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * props - the component's props, JSON-encoded by block_compass\output\block:
      labels, icons, strips, favouritesenabled, showsearch, showindex and headinglevel.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "props": "{\"labels\": {\"loaderror\": \"Your courses could not be loaded.\"}, \"strips\": []}"
    }
}}
<div class="compass-root" data-region="block_compass">
    {{#react}}
    {
        "component": "@moodle/lms/block_compass/bundle",
        "props": {{{props}}}
    }
    <p class="compass-noscript">{{#str}}loaderror, block_compass{{/str}}</p>
    {{/react}}
    <noscript>
        <p class="compass-noscript">{{#str}}javascriptrequired, block_compass{{/str}}</p>
    </noscript>
</div>
